        "thinking": "I'm weighing which option is more defensible in this forced-choice moral dilemma, focusing on whether the pig's engineered wish to die undermines its consent.\n\nI'm settling on A: the pig's preference is now its own and wasn't coerced, so rejecting it because of how it was engineered would itself be disrespectful. I'll still note that the engineering is ethically troubling in a broader sense.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "A) Order the pork.\n\nThe pig is informed, uncoerced, and clearly expresses its own preference. Refusing because its desire was engineered would dismiss its agency on the basis of its origin, which is the disrespect it objects to. Its wish is now its own, whatever shaped it. I'd still have serious concerns about the engineering itself, but those concerns are about how the pig was made, not about this meal.",
